  m_Name: SheepInfo
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  displayName: Sheep
  category: 1
  summary: Sheep give us meat, milk and wool! They stick together in flocks and usually
    follow a leader.
  facts:
  - Every spring, wool sheep get a haircut! Farmers shear off their fleece to make
    wool.
  - Baby sheep are called lambs. They can follow their moms just a day or two after
    they're born!
  - How do you tell sheep and goats apart? Sheep never have beards, but goats often
    do!
  sources:
  - Britannica for Students (Britannica Kids). Sheep. https://kids.britannica.com/students/article/sheep/277023
